WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:07.219
Today is October 02, 2026.

3
00:00:07.219 --> 00:00:12.831
Overnight, Wall Street staged a dramatic intraday recovery to close essentially flat.

4
00:00:12.831 --> 00:00:19.400
The S and P 500 managed a fractional gain, while the Nasdaq and the Dow closed near breakeven.

5
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:26.875
Early selling pushed benchmark yields sharply higher, with intermediate paper spiking toward five point six nine percent.

6
00:00:26.875 --> 00:00:33.665
An unexpected jump in the ISM manufacturing prices paid index revived persistent inflation worries.

7
00:00:33.665 --> 00:00:40.773
Initial jobless claims printed at a lean one hundred ninety-seven thousand, underscoring resilient labor conditions.

8
00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:47.537
Sentiment reversed after Fed Vice Chair Jefferson signaled a likely pause for the upcoming October policy meeting.

9
00:00:47.537 --> 00:00:54.388
Markets now price October rate hike odds below twenty-four percent, giving beaten-down equities breathing room.

10
00:00:54.388 --> 00:01:01.765
The S and P successfully defended its fifty-day moving average, holding firmly above seventy-six hundred support.

11
00:01:01.765 --> 00:01:09.939
Both JPMorgan and Morgan Stanley argue underlying corporate earnings remain intact, framing current pullbacks as healthy digestion.

12
00:01:09.939 --> 00:01:16.974
Yet bond market discipline continues to dictate institutional risk appetite across broad tech and capital goods.

13
00:01:16.974 --> 00:01:24.670
Hyperscaler artificial intelligence capex remains at unprecedented highs, sustaining high-density compute demands.

14
00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:31.471
Capital is rotating out of yield-sensitive defensives straight back into mission-critical hardware and optical networking.

15
00:01:31.471 --> 00:01:39.179
Senate proposals targeting foreign optical transceivers have sparked aggressive institutional bids for domestic vendors like Coherent.

16
00:01:39.179 --> 00:01:47.035
Meanwhile, Broadcom secures long-term ASIC dominance through a forty-two billion dollar convertible financing deal with Anthropic.

17
00:01:47.035 --> 00:01:51.398
Now, let us dive into our pivotal single stocks on watch.

18
00:01:51.398 --> 00:01:58.383
First up is Micron Technology, ticker M-U, which delivered an absolute masterclass in quarterly earnings.

19
00:01:58.383 --> 00:02:04.167
Revenue exploded nearly fourfold year-over-year to fifty-four point two billion dollars.

20
00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:11.618
Gross margins reached a staggering eighty-seven percent, while datacenter high-bandwidth memory sales surged eleven-fold.

21
00:02:11.618 --> 00:02:18.849
Management confirmed seventy-five percent of production is fully locked under long-term client contracts through 2028.

22
00:02:18.849 --> 00:02:24.939
Yet shares saw wild intraday volatility, dipping before recovering to close up three percent.

23
00:02:24.939 --> 00:02:30.969
The friction stems from next quarter margin guidance coming in just below peak whisper expectations.

24
00:02:30.969 --> 00:02:37.856
Wall Street price targets range aggressively up to nineteen hundred dollars, though Goldman Sachs sits at twelve-fifty.

25
00:02:37.856 --> 00:02:44.449
Key support rests at one thousand ten dollars, with critical downside risk managed near nine hundred.

26
00:02:44.449 --> 00:02:50.564
Next is Alphabet, ticker G-O-O-G, navigating a complex technological crosscurrent.

27
00:02:50.564 --> 00:02:58.015
The tech giant unveiled Gemini Four Argon, dominating benchmark tests across coding and enterprise workloads.

28
00:02:58.015 --> 00:03:05.625
However, shares finished lower on the day, reflecting Wall Street's shift from technical benchmarks to commercial monetization.

29
00:03:05.625 --> 00:03:13.493
With enterprise rollouts still limited, investors demand concrete token billing and margin accretion rather than raw lab scores.

30
00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:21.692
Fundamentally, Alphabet trades at an attractive twenty-one times forward earnings, backed by Berkshire Hathaway expanding its position.

31
00:03:21.692 --> 00:03:29.339
Technically, Alphabet sits at three hundred thirty-five dollars, with a solid accumulation floor at three hundred seventeen.

32
00:03:29.339 --> 00:03:38.125
Finally, Amazon, ticker A-M-Z-N, remains pinned near two hundred forty-eight dollars as cloud capex scrutiny intensifies.

33
00:03:38.125 --> 00:03:47.586
Free cash flow optic concerns persist, yet valuation near twenty-three times forward earnings offers asymmetric risk-reward at two-thirty-nine support.

34
00:03:47.586 --> 00:03:51.594
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

35
00:03:51.594 --> 00:03:55.760
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
